SDLPoP @VERSION@ for AmigaOS 3.x (AmiCradle)
=====================================================

SDLPoP is the open-source port of Jordan Mechner's Prince of Persia
(1989), made from the disassembly of the DOS game. This is its AmigaOS 3.x
build for a 68040 or 68060 with an FPU, with SDL 2 through GFOpenGPU.
Status: TESTING, not a release.

Requirements
------------

- AmigaOS 3.2, a 68040 or 68060 with an FPU, AmiCradle or an RTG board.
- GFOpenGPU's SDL2.module and SDL2_image.module in LIBS:GFOpenGPU/
  (SDL2.module from gfopenrtg's main of 2 November 2026 or later, for the
  game's own 320x200 screen).
- AHI for sound. GFOpenInput for pads (lowlevel.library alone gives the
  joystick port).
- The Prince of Persia game data (not in this archive): see
  data/ReadMe.txt.

Installing
----------

Unpack the archive where you keep games (lha x sdlpop-...lha Games:),
then put the game data in the drawer's data drawer. Settings, saves,
replays and screenshots go to the drawer's User drawer, made on the first
start. Nothing is written anywhere else.

Playing
-------

- Double-click the prince icon, or from a Shell: Stack 262144, cd to the
  drawer, then prince. Options: window (a window on the Workbench),
  full, mute, fps (the frame rate and sound buffers in the log),
  megahit N (start at level N, with cheats).
- The game starts on a 320x200 screen of its own. Alt+Return switches to
  a window and back. SDLPoP.ini holds the rest of the settings; the menu
  (Escape) changes most of them in the game.
- Keys: the cursor keys run, jump and crouch; Shift with them steps
  carefully, grabs a ledge and fights. Escape is the menu, F6 quick-saves
  and F9 loads, Space shows the time left, Ctrl+A restarts the level,
  Ctrl+G saves the game (from level 3; Ctrl+L on the title loads it),
  Ctrl+Q quits. Help takes a screenshot (the Amiga has no F12).
- Pads: the fire button is Shift and the second button jumps; the d-pad
  or stick moves. A CD32 pad's Play opens the menu.

Licence
-------

SDLPoP is GPL-3.0-or-later (COPYING.txt); its source is at
https://github.com/NagyD/SDLPoP. The Prince of Persia data is the
original game's and is not part of this archive. The icons are drawn
from SDLPoP's own program icon.

